This new route will allow you to write or replace content in a Notion page by title. Here's how it works:

1. The route accepts three parameters:
   - `title`: The title of the page to search for or create
   - `content`: The content to write
   - `replace`: Boolean flag (default: false) - when true, it will replace existing content rather than append

2. Functionality:
   - First searches for an existing page with the matching title using the enhanced title extraction
   - If no match is found, creates a new page with the specified title and content
   - If a match is found:
     - When `replace=true`: Deletes all existing blocks (except the title block) then adds the new content
     - When `replace=false`: Appends the new content to the existing page

3. The response includes:
   - Whether the operation was successful
   - Whether a new page was created or an existing one was updated
   - Whether content was replaced or appended
   - The ID of the page that was modified

You can use this endpoint with a PUT request to `/notion/write-page-by-title` like this:

```javascript
// Example to replace all content in a page
fetch('/notion/write-page-by-title', {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    title: "My Project Notes",
    content: "These are my updated notes.",
    replace: true
  })
})

// Example to append content
fetch('/notion/write-page-by-title', {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    title: "My Project Notes",
    content: "Additional notes to append."
  })
})
```

